WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.756
ALEXIS MOUSSINE-POUCHKINE:
Cloud Console

00:00:01.756 --> 00:00:03.600
is our powerful,
all-in-one graphical tool

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.930
to manage your Google Cloud
Platform resources, regardless

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:08.690
of their data center location.

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:11.430
In this video, we'll
cover the core features

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:13.410
to get you ready
to build and manage

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.070
your applications on GCP.

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:15.820
Let's get started.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:18.766
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:24.910
GCP resources are the
fundamental components

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.070
that make up the
Google Cloud Services.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:29.110
Typical examples
include Compute Engine

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:32.350
virtual machines,
Cloud Pub/Sub topics,

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:36.064
cloud storage buckets, App
Engine instances, and so forth.

00:00:36.064 --> 00:00:38.770
Resources are organized
hierarchically

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:40.810
using projects and folders.

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:42.640
Projects allow to
group resources

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.000
together and are the first
level of that hierarchy.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.740
All resources must belong
to exactly one project.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:51.400
So a given virtual machine
or Kubernetes engine cluster

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.140
belongs to one project.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:56.650
Optionally, projects can
belong to organizations,

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:58.990
and provide centralized
visibility and control

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:01.450
across all projects
in a given org.

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:04.569
You can further organize your
company departments or teams

00:01:04.569 --> 00:01:05.740
into folders.

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:08.440
Folders can contain both
projects and subfolders

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:10.660
for added flexibility.

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:13.700
This entire hierarchy
offers an ownership chain,

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:16.210
which means that when
you delete a parent,

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:19.360
all its resources
are also deleted.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:21.970
It also provides the basis
for access control policy

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:23.230
inheritance.

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:25.810
You can easily navigate
across your GCP projects

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:28.540
using the scope picker
in Cloud Console.

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:30.700
Switching projects
will tailor the view

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:34.240
to that project and all
of its child resources.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:37.870
GCP services are accessible
in the left-hand navigation

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:42.220
menu, organized by product area,
including big data, compute,

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:44.510
networking, and so forth.

00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:47.560
The home dashboard provides
a high-level overview

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:49.840
of the selected GCP
project, highlighting

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:53.330
key metrics, billing, and
other useful information.

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:55.060
You can customize
your dashboard freely.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:58.450
Any card can be hidden, shown,
and reordered on the page.

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:00.190
With the Activity
Stream, you'll be

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:02.320
able to understand all
the activities that

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:05.771
occur across your GCP
resources in one place.

00:02:05.771 --> 00:02:07.270
You can see which
projects have been

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:10.180
updated, what your
teammates are doing,

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:13.390
or audit access to
your GCP resources.

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:14.980
You can also filter
through the feed

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:16.450
to find exactly what you need.

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:19.750
The search bar in Cloud Console
allows you to quickly access

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:23.020
Google Cloud Platform products
and any of your resources

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:24.370
across GCP.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.830
Simply search for App
Engine or the name

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:28.480
of one of your projects.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:31.240
The APIs and Services
section of the Console

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:34.570
is where you can manage one
of our hundreds of APIs,

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:38.530
enable or disable a service,
generate or revoke credentials,

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:40.900
monitor requests, and so forth.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:44.560
This includes all of our GCP,
machine learning, Google Maps,

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:47.080
G Suite, and Analytics APIs.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:48.910
If you ever get
stuck or need help

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:52.570
navigating the world of GCP, our
support team is here to help.

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:55.570
Your support cases relating
to both development questions

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:58.330
and production issues
are all accessible right

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:00.880
from the Console
navigation menu.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:05.110
Google Cloud Identity and
Access Management, or Cloud IAM,

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:07.450
enables you to manage
and create permissions

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:08.800
for your GCP resources.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.480
As your team grows,
you can grant access

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:13.370
to teammates using the
IAM and Admin section.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:16.240
Add users, groups,
or service accounts,

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:17.980
and assign them
any number of roles

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:19.622
to grant them the
permission they need.

00:03:19.622 --> 00:03:21.580
As you can see, there
are many predefined roles

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:25.360
to choose from, not just
admin and developer.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:28.570
Google Cloud Shell provides
you with command line access

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:31.330
to your cloud resources
directly from your browser.

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:33.700
You can easily manage your
projects and resources

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:36.040
without having to install
anything on your system.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:38.700
Cloud Shell is accessible
right from your browser

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:41.710
in Cloud Console, and is powered
by a small virtual machine

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:45.190
with persistent disk space and
up-to-date software for all

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:46.780
of your development needs.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:49.240
It even comes with a web editor.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:51.760
The billing section
of the cloud console

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.800
is where you manage
billing accounts

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.510
and link your projects to them.

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:58.420
A billing account is
essentially a payment method--

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:00.820
one or more credit card
information or bank

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:01.810
account details.

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:03.730
A project that does not
have billing enabled--

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:06.310
that means it does not have any
associated billing account--

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:08.320
will just not be able
to use GCP products

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:09.454
beyond their free tiers.

00:04:09.454 --> 00:04:10.870
You can change the
billing account

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:13.220
for a given project
at any point in time.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:16.269
You can set budget alerts
to help you manage costs,

00:04:16.269 --> 00:04:19.610
and set up triggered actions for
projects or accounts, as well.

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:22.240
You can also generate
billing exports, as well as

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:24.820
reports to better
understand your spend.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:28.960
Finally, Cloud Console is also
available as a free mobile app

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:30.820
for both Android and iOS.

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:33.370
It can help you understand
the health of your services

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:36.290
at a glance with
customizable graphs--

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:39.730
CPU, network usage,
QPS, and so forth--

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:41.260
and show you any billing alerts.

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:44.050
It allows you to manage
incidents and alerts,

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:47.180
navigate through error
and crash reports.

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:50.230
You can also start and stop
Compute Engine instances,

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:53.590
navigate through their logs,
and even SSH into them.

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:56.440
Other products such as
App Engine, Cloud Storage,

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:58.780
and Cloud SQL are
also supported.

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:02.140
I can't wait to see what you
build next with Cloud Console.

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:04.930
If you like this video, please
like, subscribe, comment,

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:09.390
share, and look forward to
more GCP Essentials videos.

